# The evaluation corpus is data with character offsets into it (evals/datasets/retrieval/retrieval.jsonl spans): every
# checkout must hold the same bytes, so it is LF on every platform (a Windows autocrlf checkout once shifted every span
# and failed CI on Linux).
evals/corpus/** text eol=lf

# Documents are bytes: never convert line endings inside a PDF or DOCX. seed/'s `* text eol=lf` once stripped the CR
# bytes inside the demo PDFs, so the committed seed copies no longer matched their recorded originals (seed:check).
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
# The recorded demo's documents are copied into seed/ byte for byte, so a Windows checkout must not add CRs to them.
frontend/scripts/seed-build/recorded/knowledge-files/** -text
